<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank sets cash reserve requirements.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank sets cash reserve requirements.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said it would set a compulsory cash reserve requirement for the money market at 5.156 billion guilders for the period from Feb 14 to Feb 28.</p>
<p>The new reserve is unchanged from the previous 14-day cash reserve.</p>
<p>The compulsory cash reserve for commercial banks is one of several instruments the central bank uses to steer money market liquidity and short term interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
